---js
{
  layout: "layouts/base.webc",
  meta: {
    title: "Support matrix",
    description: "Which DynamoDB emulators support which operations - a per-area grid across every target, from the latest run.",
  },
  // The matrix is built from the latest run, so its freshness tracks the data,
  // not this file's git date. Keeps the sitemap <lastmod> honest.
  eleventyComputed: {
    lastmod: (data) => data.conformance?.latest?.date,
  },
}
---
<section class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-12">
  <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 dark:text-white mb-2">Support across emulators</h1>
  <p class="text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300 mb-5 max-w-3xl">
    Each operation area, against every target, from the latest run.
  </p>

  <!-- Definitions double as the glyph legend, one per line so the meanings stay readable. -->
  <dl class="mb-5 max-w-3xl space-y-2.5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <div class="flex gap-2.5">
      <dt class="flex w-28 shrink-0 items-baseline gap-1.5">
        <span class="font-bold text-pass-700 dark:text-pass-400" aria-hidden="true">✓</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Supported</span>
      </dt>
      <dd>every test in that area passes.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="flex gap-2.5">
      <dt class="flex w-28 shrink-0 items-baseline gap-1.5">
        <span class="font-bold text-partial-700 dark:text-partial-400" aria-hidden="true">◑</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Partial</span>
      </dt>
      <dd>the target implements the operation but doesn't match it exactly: some tests pass, some fail or skip, so one edge-case gap doesn't drag a whole operation into the red.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="flex gap-2.5">
      <dt class="flex w-28 shrink-0 items-baseline gap-1.5">
        <span class="font-bold text-fail-700 dark:text-fail-400" aria-hidden="true">✗</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Failing</span>
      </dt>
      <dd>the operation is implemented but passes nothing at all.</dd>
    </div>
    <div class="flex gap-2.5">
      <dt class="flex w-28 shrink-0 items-baseline gap-1.5">
        <span class="font-bold text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400" aria-hidden="true">–</span>
        <span class="font-medium text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-200">Unsupported</span>
      </dt>
      <dd>the target doesn't implement it.</dd>
    </div>
  </dl>

  <p class="mb-8 max-w-3xl text-sm text-zinc-500 dark:text-zinc-400">
    Hover a cell for the exact pass, fail and skip counts.
  </p>

  <!-- The grid appears only once it fits: 7 targets at 7rem plus the operation
       column needs about 980px, which lg is the first breakpoint to give. Below
       that it folds to one card per operation.
       It used to fold at sm, which left a wide band of screen widths showing a
       table scrolled sideways with three targets off the edge and nothing to
       say so. Scrollbars are hidden until used on macOS, so the columns were
       not missing, they were invisible. -->
  <div class="hidden lg:block">
    <support-matrix :matrix="supportMatrix($data.conformance)"></support-matrix>
  </div>
  <div class="lg:hidden space-y-8" @html="supportCards($data.conformance)"></div>

  <suggest-target></suggest-target>
</section>
